  "ref": "JDG.11.34",
  "review_notes": [
    "`יְחִידָה` must hold the *only*, since rule 31 forbids heading its unit on the supplied generic *child*; `רַק` is then the unrendered occurrence. Giving *only* to `רַק` and leaving `יְחִידָה` a bare *child* was the competing reading.",
    "*neither ... nor* is the written correlative pair: the existential negative takes the opening word and `אוֹ` the closing one (rule 14)."
  ]
